{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Enrique Malek International Airport (IATA: DAV, ICAO: MPDA) ("Spanish: Aeropuerto Internacional Enrique Malek") is an international airport located in the city of David, Chiriquí in the Republic of Panama.","title":"Enrique Malek International Airport"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The former terminal was demolished for a new one to be built.","title":"Enrique Malek International Airport"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" When construction had finished, daily flights from Air Panama started arriving.","title":"Enrique Malek International Airport"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Now the international flight terminal receives numerous daily flights from Copa Airlines and Air Panama.","title":"Enrique Malek International Airport"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Also car rentals commenced operations in the new terminal.","title":"Enrique Malek International Airport"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Australian Two Airlines Policy (or Two Airlines Agreement) was a policy of Australian Federal Governments from the late 1940s to the 1990s.","title":"Two Airlines Policy"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Under the policy, only two airlines were allowed to operate flights between state capital city and major regional city airports. For most of the period of the policy, the "two airlines" were the privately owned Ansett Airlines and the government-owned Trans Australia Airlines.","title":"Two Airlines Policy"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Though persisting for some decades, the policy finally fell into abeyance in the world-wide airline deregulations of the 1990s.","title":"Two Airlines Policy"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Air Panama is a regional airline based at Albrook "Marcos A. Gelabert" International Airport in Panama, and is currently the second-largest air carrier in the country, surpassed only by Copa Airlines.","title":"Air Panama"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The carrier offers both scheduled and charter passenger flights to more than 31 destinations from its hub at