 claim Chinese ancestry.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Nearly all Chinese nationals in Samoa reside within the Apia municipal area; neighbouring American Samoa, also has a small population of Chinese expatriates.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Samoas Legislative Capital city of Apia signed a treaty on 31:08:2015 with a delegation from Shenzhen, China making the Legislative capital of Apia and The city of Shenzhen, Guangdong, China sister cities.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The treaty will help bring Chinese tourists to boast Samoas growing Tourism industry and will also bring economic growth to Samoa also bringing stronger ties between the two cities.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Shenzhen Airlines is also set to operate flights from Shenzhen International airport and Faleolo International Airport, Apia.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The Chinese community in Samoa is growing and becoming economically strong.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" A new wave of Chinese migrants moving to Samoa are coming from the northern region, bringing their culture and languages with them.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" There are no Chinese schools in Samoa but an estimated 98.7% of Chinese expatriates and migrants send their children and youth to Robert Louis Stevenson School, Samoa which is a private school with an Australasian and Samoan curriculum, the tuition fee is WST700-845.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" There is a primary campus located in the village of Lotopa, Faleata District and the secondary campus in the urban village of Tafaigata.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"},{"sentence_id":10,"text":" Notable Chinese businesses include Frankie's Supermarket and Wholesale, Alan wholesale and Treasure Garden company as well as other small businesses and restaurants.","title":"Chinese in Samoa"}